    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a limited footprint, as the core of our roster\u2014including elite anchors **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014are sidelined by a team off-day. Consequently, our offensive output hinges on a thin two-man showing: **Liam Hicks** (53.91) and **Brayan Rocchio** (47.20). **Liam Hicks** serves as our strongest play; he draws a favorable matchup against Shawn Armstrong (4.35 xERA), and despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status, his assumed #4 spot provides a substantial boost to his base projection. His efficiency is bolstered by a strong platoon advantage against the right-handed Armstrong, positioning him as the primary focal point for run production in an otherwise quiet day for the club.\n\n**Brayan Rocchio** rounds out the lineup, though his viability remains marginal. While he benefits from the weak 4.63 xERA of Nick Martinez, he suffers from the expected #9 spot in the batting order, which suppresses his run-scoring potential. The decision to start **Brayan Rocchio** over our deep bench was dictated strictly by volume; with **Luis Robert Jr.** officially sidelined on the IL, we are protecting our game caps while ensuring we don't cede total production. Looking ahead, we need to monitor the lineup confirmation for **Liam Hicks** closely; if he shifts out of the cleanup spot, his score will require a recalibration, but for now, his platoon-adjusted ceiling is the only viable path to meaningful Roto point gains today.",
